      "problem": "Which of the following plots is the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n- The domain is all real numbers except $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n.$\n\n- The range is all real numbers, so there is no minimum or maximum.\n\n- The period of the function is $\\pi .$\n\n- Its zeros occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n.$\n\n- $y\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to {\\pi }^{-},$ and $y\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254348/assets/22674bef9e806fca07026b8d441877c251761de4c64cc005eed912e62a34ce67.png)",
